 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of Peekskill to impose hotel or motel taxes within such city",
    "basePrintNo": "S5940",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5940-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-aa, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5940\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of\nPeekskill to impose hotel or motel taxes within such city\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis bill would amend the Tax Law to permit the City of Peekskill to\nimpose a hotel or motel tax.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would add a new section Section 1206-aa to the Tax Law to\nauthorize the City of Peekskill to adopt and amend its local laws to\nimpose a tax upon hotel and motel rooms in the City of Peekskill.\n\nThe rate of such a tax would not be permitted to not exceed three\npercent (3%) of the per diem rental rate for each room, and that it is\nnot applicable to a permanent resident of a hotel or motel.\n\nThe tax would be collected and administered by the chief fiscal\nofficer of the City of Peekskill and in the same manner as other taxes\nare now collected and administered. Local laws may provide for the\nfiling of returns and the payment of the tax on a monthly basis or on\nthe basis of any longer or shorter period of time.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCurrently, the City of Peekskill does not impose a tax on visitors who\nstay in hotels or motels within the City.  The City of Peekskill has\nrequested the authority to impose a motel/hotel tax. This bill would\naccommodate the request of their city council.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone for the State but will increase taxes and revenues for the City\nof Peekskill.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
